-- title:
--   Finite freeness of rank p^{vh} of 𝒪[[X]]/([p^v]_F)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime number such that $(p:\mathcal O)$ is a non-zero-divisor, the ideal $(p)=\mathrm{span}\{p\}$ is maximal, and $\mathcal O$ is adically complete for $(p)$; write $k=\mathcal O/(p)$. Let $d\in\mathbb N$ and let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal O$, i.e. a $d$-tuple of power series in the $2d$ variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d\oplus\mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant terms, with the two families of linear coefficients given by the identity matrix, and satisfying associativity in the sense of the two iterated substitutions in $3d$ variables agreeing. For $n\in\mathbb N$ let $F.\mathtt{nthSeries}\,n$ be the $d$-tuple of power series in $d$ variables defined by $0$ for $n=0$ and, inductively, by substituting $(F.\mathtt{nthSeries}\,n,\;X)$ into $F$ — that is, the multiplication-by-$n$ series of $F$. Let $h,v\in\mathbb N$ and assume that the quotient of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ by the ideal generated by the $d$ components of the $p^v$-th such series of the formal group law obtained from $F$ by applying the reduction map $\mathcal O\to k$ to all coefficients has $k$-dimension $p^{vh}$. Then the quotient of $\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ by the ideal generated by the $d$ components of $F.\mathtt{nthSeries}\,(p^v)$ is a finite free $\mathcal O$-module of rank $p^{vh}$.
--
--   This is the statement that the affine algebra of the $p^v$-torsion of a formal group of finite height $h$ over a $p$-adically complete discrete valuation ring is finite and free of rank $p^{vh}$, the freeness being deduced from the fact that the multiplication-by-$p^v$ components together with $p$ form a system of parameters, hence a regular sequence, in the regular local ring $\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$. It is used to produce the corresponding unique decomposition of power series along a basis of this quotient.
